# Third-party components / 第三方组件聲明

The EFI in this repository bundles prebuilt third-party kernel extensions.
They are redistributed here ONLY as configuration data for this platform
build; each kext remains the property of its authors. Always prefer the
official upstream releases:

| Kext | Version (bundled) | Bundle ID | Upstream |
|------|-------------------|-----------|----------|
| Lilu.kext | 1.7.3 | as.vit9696.Lilu | https://github.com/acidanthera/Lilu (BSD-3-Clause) |
| VirtualSMC.kext | 1.3.9 | as.vit9696.VirtualSMC | https://github.com/acidanthera/VirtualSMC (BSD-3-Clause) |
| SMCProcessor.kext | 1.3.9 | as.vit9696.SMCProcessor | https://github.com/acidanthera/VirtualSMC (BSD-3-Clause) |
| SMCSuperIO.kext | 1.3.9 | ru.joedm.SMCSuperIO | https://github.com/acidanthera/VirtualSMC (BSD-3-Clause) |
| WhateverGreen.kext | 1.7.2 | as.vit9696.WhateverGreen | https://github.com/acidanthera/WhateverGreen (BSD-3-Clause) |
| RestrictEvents.kext | 1.1.7 | as.vit9696.RestrictEvents | https://github.com/acidanthera/RestrictEvents (BSD-3-Clause) |
| USBToolBox.kext | (see Info.plist) | com.dhinakg.USBToolBox.kext | https://github.com/USBToolBox/kext (MIT) |
| UTBDefault.kext | 1.0 | com.dhinakg.USBToolBox.injector | Generated by https://github.com/USBToolBox/tool |
| IntelMausiEthernet.kext | 3.0.3 | com.insanelymac.IntelMausiEthernet | https://github.com/SergeyIschenko/IntelMausiEthernet (upstream as stated) |
| CtlnaAHCIPort.kext | 341.0.2 | com.apple.driver.CtlnaAHCIPort | Third-party community kext; see Info.plist and upstream distribution |
| XHCI-unsupported.kext | 0.9.2 | org.rehabman.injector.XHCI.unsupported | https://github.com/Mieze/XHCI-unsupported? see upstream (rehabman distribution) |

OpenCore binaries (OpenCore.efi / BOOTX64.efi / OpenRuntime.efi / HfsPlus.efi /
apfs_aligned.efi / ResetNvramEntry.efi) are **NOT included** in this public
release. Take them from:
- OpenCore (official): https://github.com/acidanthera/OpenCorePkg/releases
- HfsPlus.efi: https://github.com/acidanthera/OcBinaryData
See Docs/ for the exact file mapping used by the author's verified setup.

The SSDT *.aml files under OC/ACPI are standard Coffee Lake platform SSDTs
compiled AMLs; review and rebuild from sources if you need changes.
